---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Navigation from '../components/Navigation.astro';
---

<Layout title="Terms of Service - FanConnect">
  <Navigation />
  <main class="terms-page">
    <div class="container">
      <h1>Terms of Service</h1>
      <p class="updated">Effective: March 2026</p>

      <section>
        <h2>1. What this is</h2>
        <p>
          FanConnect is a platform where creators publish content and subscribers
          pay to access it. By using FanConnect you agree to these terms. If you
          don't agree, don't use the platform.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>2. You must be 18+</h2>
        <p>
          You must be at least 18 years old to create an account, subscribe,
          or post content. We will terminate accounts that we believe belong
          to anyone under 18.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>3. Your account</h2>
        <p>
          You're responsible for your account and everything that happens on it.
          Use a strong password, don't share your credentials, and let us know
          immediately if you think someone else has accessed your account.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>4. Creator responsibilities</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>You own the content you upload, or you have a valid licence for it.</li>
          <li>Every person in your content is 18+ and has given documented consent.</li>
          <li>You comply with our <a href="/guidelines">Community Guidelines</a> at all times.</li>
          <li>You're responsible for paying taxes on your earnings. We're not your accountant.</li>
          <li>You don't make promises to subscribers you can't keep.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>5. Subscriber responsibilities</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Don't redistribute, re-upload, or share content you've paid for. It's not yours to distribute.</li>
          <li>Don't screen-record or screenshot content to share elsewhere.</li>
          <li>Don't harass creators through comments or messages.</li>
          <li>Chargebacks for content you accessed and consumed are not okay.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>6. Payments</h2>
        <p>
          Payments are processed through Stripe. Subscription fees are billed monthly.
          Creators receive their earnings minus our platform fee. Refund requests
          are handled case-by-case — we're fair about it, but we don't do blanket refunds
          for content you've already viewed.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>7. Content ownership</h2>
        <p>
          You keep ownership of what you upload. By posting on FanConnect, you give
          us a licence to host, display, and distribute it through the platform.
          That licence ends when you delete your content or close your account.
          We don't sell your content or use it for anything outside the platform.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>8. Takedowns and removal</h2>
        <p>
          We respond to valid copyright takedown requests. If you're featured in
          content and want it removed, contact us with proof of identity. Creators
          who repeatedly ignore takedown requests will be banned.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>9. Termination</h2>
        <p>
          We can suspend or terminate accounts that violate these terms or our
          community guidelines. If we ban you for a zero-tolerance violation
          (see <a href="/guidelines">guidelines</a>), any pending earnings may
          be forfeited. You can also delete your account at any time through settings.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>10. Liability</h2>
        <p>
          We provide the platform as-is. We do our best to keep things running
          and your data safe, but we can't guarantee 100% uptime or that nothing
          will ever go wrong. We're not liable for content posted by users — that's
          on them. If you see something that shouldn't be here, report it and we'll
          deal with it.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>11. Changes</h2>
        <p>
          We may update these terms. When we do, we'll post the new version here
          and update the date at the top. Continuing to use the platform means
          you accept the updated terms.
        </p>
      </section>

      <div class="terms-footer">
        <p>Questions about these terms? Email <a href="mailto:legal@fanconnect.com">legal@fanconnect.com</a></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>
</Layout>

<style>
  .terms-page {
    margin-top: 60px;
    min-height: calc(100vh - 60px);
    background: #f8f9fa;
  }

  .container {
    max-width: 800px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 3rem 2rem;
  }

  h1 {
    font-size: 2.5rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: #1a1a1a;
    margin: 0 0 0.5rem 0;
  }

  .updated {
    color: #999;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    margin-bottom: 3rem;
  }

  section {
    margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
  }

  h2 {
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: #1a1a1a;
    margin: 0 0 0.75rem 0;
  }

  p {
    color: #444;
    line-height: 1.7;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }

  ul {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.5rem;
  }

  li {
    color: #444;
    line-height: 1.6;
    padding-left: 1.5rem;
    position: relative;
  }

  li::before {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    top: 0.6rem;
    width: 6px;
    height: 6px;
    background: #667eea;
    border-radius: 50%;
  }

  a {
    color: #667eea;
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .terms-footer {
    margin-top: 3rem;
    padding-top: 2rem;
    border-top: 1px solid #e0e0e0;
    text-align: center;
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .container {
      padding: 2rem 1rem;
    }

    h1 {
      font-size: 2rem;
    }
  }
</style>
